# Next.js / project conventions (boss-web)

This repo runs **Next.js 16 + React 19**. APIs differ from older training data — when unsure about a Next API, check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing code, and heed deprecation notices.

## Server vs client

- Server Components are the default. Add `"use client"` only when the component needs state, effects, browser APIs, or event handlers.
- Server mutations live in `actions.ts` files (`"use server"`). Keep secrets and admin Supabase access on the server side only.
- `async`/`await` the dynamic APIs that are now async (`cookies()`, `headers()`, route `params`/`searchParams`).

## Imports & structure

- Use the `@/` path alias for absolute imports.
- `app/` = routes/pages/actions, `lib/` = shared logic (pricing, supabase, email, xero), `components/` = shared UI, `scripts/` = node maintenance/import scripts, `data/` = supplier data, `supabase/` = migrations + SQL.

## Workflow expectations

- Build runs codegen first (`prebuild` regenerates SKUs/titles). Don't hand-edit generated outputs; change the generator under `scripts/` instead.
- After non-trivial changes: `npm run lint` and `npm run test:run` (TZ is pinned to Australia/Perth in test/build scripts — keep date logic timezone-safe).
- Commits to `main` auto-deploy via Vercel. Only commit when the user asks. Never commit `.env.local` or service-role keys.
- Time-sensitive logic should respect `TZ=Australia/Perth` (the store's timezone), not the local machine.
